- U3: それでいい
  - A: Implemented the approved durable fix in the wrapper and native build-environment verifier. Added host OpenSSL, pinned xkbcommon, version-qualified requirements, mixed-route, unknown-package, and single-argument package-smuggling checks. A fresh independent review found and drove fixes for version-qualified system-deps arguments and single-argument route bypasses; the final delta review reported no important findings. Verified bash syntax, native routing, mise run check, a clean temporary dioxus-cli 0.7.10 install, and two complete mise run test executions, with the final exact diff completing in 90.45 seconds. Committed only the two scripts as 5ae3f2c389a0e2ec89bc825a4e0b7db31a70876d, then completed mise run build. Did not push or rerun GitHub Actions because remote writes were not authorized. The durable invariant is already encoded in the wrapper and executable verification, so no additional guidance change was proposed.
